From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Pakuła <tomasz.pakula.oficjalny@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Jan 2026 21:31:36 +0000
Subject: Input: Introduce EV_BTN event for generic buttons

This will be used to fire generic button events that only transmit
button number and it's value, not related to any defined usage.

Made for HID joysticks but could be adopted by other devices.

Signed-off-by: Tomasz Pakuła <tomasz.pakula.oficjalny@gmail.com>

[ORDER 15: carried unchanged from Tomasz Pakuła's "[RFC PATCH n/6] Input: New EV_BTN event for generic buttons", linux-input and LKML, 2026-01-04 (the newest posted version; no v2 by 2026-11-06, not in torvalds/linux master of 2026-11-06).
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260104213132.163904-1-tomasz.pakula.oficjalny@gmail.com/
Archive copy of this patch: https://lkml.iu.edu/2601.0/01919.html
Review so far: Benjamin Tissoires 2026-01-08 asks for a different shape of patches 3 and 4 (map the HID Button usage page to EV_BTN directly, EV_BTN only for that page, keep the existing EV_KEY mapping without the upper bound); Peter Hutterer 2026-01-08 and Randy Dunlap 2026-01-04 (documentation wording of patch 1); Ivan Gorinov 2026-01-07 (EVIOCGKEY-like read of the initial state). The author has not posted a revision; this group is the text as posted and is replaced by the author's next version when it is posted.
Applies to v7.3.1 without change of any hunk.
Drop this group when the series, in the author's or the maintainers' final form, is in the release this kernel moves to.]
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 Documentation/input/event-codes.rst    | 5 +++++
 include/uapi/linux/input-event-codes.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/input/event-codes.rst b/Documentation/input/event-codes.rst
index 4424cbff251f..c387eaa63dfb 100644
--- a/Documentation/input/event-codes.rst
+++ b/Documentation/input/event-codes.rst
@@ -59,6 +59,11 @@ Codes section for details on valid codes for each type.
 
   - Used to describe binary state input switches.
 
+* EV_BTN:
+
+  - Used to describe state changes generic, numbered buttons without defined
+    usages.
+
 * EV_LED:
 
   - Used to turn LEDs on devices on and off.
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/input-event-codes.h b/include/uapi/linux/input-event-codes.h
index 30f3c9eaafaa..1c853c37b58a 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/input-event-codes.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/input-event-codes.h
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #define EV_ABS			0x03
 #define EV_MSC			0x04
 #define EV_SW			0x05
+#define EV_BTN			0x06
 #define EV_LED			0x11
 #define EV_SND			0x12
 #define EV_REP			0x14
